@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+# Sinker (Sinker Burn, Sinker Side Burn)
+
+A 60 x 40 x 25 mm clean-room block with one blind rectangular cavity.
+The cavity is 20 x 12 mm and 8 mm deep (floor `Z17`), centred at `(5, 0)`.
+A sinker EDM burns it with one rectangular electrode.
+
+The machine is the shipped template `Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)`.
+The template states no conditions and no codes.
+The build script adds them with `edit_machine`.
+The two conditions and all of the code words are invented for this example.
+They are not the codes of any control.
+Before you use a real machine, take its conditions and codes from the control's manual.
+
+| Condition | Role | Spark gap per side | Undersize per side |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `R1` | rough | 0.10 mm | 0.25 mm |
+| `F1` | finish | 0.03 mm | 0.03 mm |
+
+## What it shows
+
+1. **Electrode (`E-19.5x11.5`):** `electrode_from_faces` makes the electrode from the cavity's floor and four walls.
+   The `R1` undersize makes it 0.25 mm smaller per side: 19.5 x 11.5 mm.
+2. **Sinker Burn (`Rough burn`, condition `R1`, pass `rough`):** The electrode sinks at `(5, 0)` in one servo block, `M101 Z17.25 F50.`.
+   A rough pass leaves 0.15 mm (0.25 undersize - 0.10 gap) on each wall and on the floor.
+   Thus the electrode tip stops at the floor + 0.15 + 0.10 = `Z17.25`.
+3. **Sinker Side Burn (`Side burn +X`, condition `F1`):** The electrode sinks again to the floor + the finish gap, `Z17.03`.
+   This takes the floor to its drawn depth.
+   Then the electrode moves 0.22 mm toward +X and back, at that depth: two `M102` blocks.
+   The move puts the +X wall at its drawn size (0.25 undersize - 0.03 finish gap = 0.22).
+   The other three walls keep the 0.15 mm rough allowance.
+
+## What to look at
+
+- In `sinker.nc`, find the two `(OPERATION: ...)` sections.
+  Each section selects its condition (`ER1`, `EF1`) before its burn.
+- Only the side burn section has `M102` blocks.
+  The first goes to `X5.22`, and the second comes back to `X5.`.
+  `Y` and `Z` do not change during the lateral move.
+- A straight burn moves the electrode in Z only.
+  A side burn moves one wall out by a stated amount.
+  CamCraft refuses an amount larger than the undersize minus the condition's gap.
+- The post refuses a Side Burn if the machine does not state the `side` code.
+
+## Files
+
+- `model/gen_sinker_obj.py` — watertight voxel-CSG generator for the block and its cavity.
+- `model/sinker.obj` — generated quad mesh imported by `build.camscript`.
+- `build.camscript` — headless script that builds `sinker.camproj` and posts `sinker.nc` through CamCraft's undoable commands.
+- `case.toml` — operation kinds, machine and expected result.
+- `sinker.camproj` — committed project with generated toolpaths.
+- `sinker.nc` — committed program, checked byte for byte in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`.
+
+## Rebuild and verify
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```sh
+cargo xtask catalog --case edm/sinker
+cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog
+```
diff --git a/examples/catalog/edm/sinker/build.camscript b/examples/catalog/edm/sinker/build.camscript
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..9c5ec1a95
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/catalog/edm/sinker/build.camscript
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+// Provenance: original sinker EDM catalog case (#2872) using CamCraft's public commands.
+// Builds sinker.camproj and posts sinker.nc headlessly through CamCraft's
+// undoable command verbs. Run with CWD = this case directory:
+//   camcraft-cli script build.camscript
+
+cam.import("model/sinker.obj", "sinker");
+cam.call("set_model_link", { model: "sinker", path: null });
+cam.call("fit_stock", { shape: "box", margin: 0.0 });
+cam.call("load_machine", { builtin: "Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)" });
+
+// The shipped template states no conditions and no codes: a real machine
+// takes them from its control's manual. These values and words are
+// invented for this example. They are not the codes of any control.
+cam.call("edit_machine", {
+  patch: {
+    edm: {
+      conditions: [
+        { id: "R1", name: "example rough", gap: 0.10, undersize: 0.25, role: "rough" },
+        { id: "F1", name: "example finish", gap: 0.03, undersize: 0.03, role: "finish" }
+      ],
+      codes: {
+        metric: "G21",
+        inch: "G20",
+        pickup: "T{tool} M06",
+        reference: "M100 H{offset}",
+        condition: "E{id}",
+        depth: "M101 Z{z} F{f}",
+        side: "M102 X{x} Y{y} Z{z} F{f}",
+        end: "M02"
+      }
+    }
+  }
+});
+cam.call("add_setup", { name: "Sinker" });
+cam.call("set_setup_post", { post: "Sinker EDM (ISO)" });
+
+// The cavity's floor and four walls: the faces inside its 20 x 12 mm box,
+// below the work top.
+var rows = cam.call("list_features", { model: "sinker", kinds: ["faces"] });
+var picks = [];
+for (var i = 0; i < rows.faces.length; i++) {
+  var f = rows.faces[i];
+  var lo = f.bounds.min, hi = f.bounds.max;
+  if (lo[0] >= -5.0 - 1e-6 && hi[0] <= 15.0 + 1e-6 && lo[1] >= -6.0 - 1e-6 && hi[1] <= 6.0 + 1e-6 && lo[2] >= 17.0 - 1e-6) {
+    picks.push({ model: "sinker", id: f.id });
+  }
+}
+if (picks.length !== 5) {
+  throw new Error("expected the cavity floor and four walls, got " + picks.length + " faces");
+}
+
+// The electrode: the cavity outline made smaller by the rough
+// condition's undersize (0.25 mm per side).
+var electrode = cam.call("electrode_from_faces", {
+  name: "E-19.5x11.5", picks: picks, condition: "R1", stub: 10.0, pickup: 15.0
+});
+
+// Sinker Burn: the rough burn sinks the electrode to the cavity floor.
+var burn = electrode.burn;
+burn.condition = "R1";
+burn.pass = "rough";
+cam.call("add_operation", {
+  kind: "Sinker Burn", name: "Rough burn", tool: "E-19.5x11.5", source: "stock", params: burn
+});
+
+// Sinker Side Burn: the finish condition burns to the floor again, then
+// moves the same electrode 0.22 mm toward +X and back. That moves the +X
+// wall out to its drawn size: 0.25 undersize - 0.03 finish gap = 0.22.
+var side = electrode.burn;
+side.condition = "F1";
+delete side.pass;
+side.direction = "plus_x";
+side.amount = 0.22;
+side.undersize = 0.25;
+cam.call("add_operation", {
+  kind: "Sinker Side Burn", name: "Side burn +X", tool: "E-19.5x11.5", source: "stock", params: side
+});
+
+cam.generate();
+var verdict = cam.verify();
+if (!verdict.ok) {
+  throw new Error("sinker catalog verify failed: " + JSON.stringify(verdict));
+}
+cam.save("sinker.camproj");
+cam.post({ to: "sinker.nc" });
+cam.report();
